# STANDALONE REMOTE-DB DEPLOYMENT.
# This app runs the DM picture reader (SniperPlug-Reader) as its own
# Discloud application, sharing the production Turso/libSQL database
# with the canonical SniperPlug app — the same pattern as the HP
# watcher. It has NO Discord connection: the bot queues picture jobs
# in the dm_ocr_jobs table with the attachment URL, this app claims
# one job at a time, downloads and reads the picture with the tuned
# rapidocr build (which provably cannot fit the bot's 256 MB
# container), writes the raw text back, and keeps a heartbeat row
# fresh — that heartbeat is how the bot knows picture reading is up.
# It requires TURSO_DATABASE_URL and TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN and fails
# closed without them. Exactly one reader should run at a time; the
# job claim is lease-guarded, so an accidental second reader cannot
# double-read, but it would waste memory.
#
# DEPLOY RECIPE (learned live 2026-11-19; do not rediscover):
# the zip is the whole repo with THIS file copied to discloud.config
# at the zip root, and the zip's requirements.txt must be the UNION
# of requirements.txt + requirements-reader.txt — Discloud installs
# requirements.txt for a Python app, and a custom-named requirements
# file in BUILD alone was not enough to get the OCR set installed.
# BUILD below names both files anyway (single command: Discloud runs
# BUILD with no shell, so never use && or ; in it). Set the Turso
# keys with env-set, then commit the zip again — stored env reaches
# the container only on a commit deploy.
#
# OpenCV: rapidocr's opencv-python wheel needs libGL, which the
# Discloud image does not have. The engine repairs this itself at
# first import (see _repair_opencv_headless in
# sniperplug/ocr_reader/engine.py); no build step is needed.
NAME=SniperPlug-Reader
TYPE=bot
MAIN=ocr_reader_main.py
RAM=512
VERSION=3.11
AUTORESTART=true
BUILD=pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-reader.txt
